  "slug": "quantum-topic-86d4",
  "summary": "Eight preprints pair compilation and fault-tolerance resource savings with Lean-checked or exact certification of circuits and codes.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is fault-tolerant quantum software where resource reduction is paired with correctness guarantees. Compilation work includes MARBLE, which synthesizes OpenQASM block encodings from matrix formulas, qlin, which rewrites dynamic-circuit branches and decoders with a Lean 4-verified translation validator, and PRISM, which keeps multiple logical-gate realizations open during dual-rail routing. Verification work includes a formally verified Shor order-finding harness with O(n^(2+ε)) gate cost, QECLean for machine-verified code specification, and QEDist for exact distance certification of stabilizer codes, including fault distance. Architecture-level papers formalize reaction depth, showing constant-depth coherent Boolean arithmetic, and use Block Checks with Pareto tree search for state-preparation depth-operation trade-offs. Formal verification is not common to every item.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
